#
# usage_daily — daily per-tenant rollup of meili_ingest_usage.
#
# Target of the materialized pipe `pipes/usage_daily_mv.pipe`; never written directly.
# Columns hold aggregate STATES, so every read must merge them
# (`sumMerge`, `countMerge`) — see `pipes/tenant_usage.pipe`.
#
# Sorting key `project_id, day, pipeline_uid, plugin` matches the rollup's GROUP BY and,
# like the raw table, leads with the tenant: billing reads one project at a time.
# Job-level rows (kind = 'job') carry no plugin, so their counters land in the
# `plugin = ''` bucket.
#
# CAVEAT (see pipes/usage_daily_mv.pipe): a materialized view fires per INSERT and does not
# see the ReplacingMergeTree deduplication of the source, so a redelivered event would
# be counted twice HERE while the raw table stays correct. The raw data source remains
# the source of truth for an invoice; this rollup is for dashboards and estimates.
#
# ── Retention: 180 days, like the raw table ─────────────────────────────────────
# A deployment that changes `usage_daily_mv`'s query rebuilds this table by re-running
# the pipe over `meili_ingest_usage`, which only holds 180 days. Tinybird therefore
# refuses that backfill unless this TTL is no longer than the source's ("it has no
# TTL, while the table that is going to be used for backfill ... has a TTL"), since a
# rebuild would silently drop every older day. With matching TTLs the rollup is a pure
# function of the raw table: any rebuild reproduces it exactly, under the new query.
# Long-term history lives in `usage_daily_billing`, which deployments never recompute.
#
# `day` is a Date, so a day's row expires at the start of day + 180, slightly ahead
# of the raw rows it summarises (`ts` + 180 days): the rollup never outlives its source.
#

SCHEMA >
    `project_id` LowCardinality(String),
    `day` Date,
    `pipeline_uid` LowCardinality(String),
    `plugin` LowCardinality(String),
    `rows_count` AggregateFunction(count),
    `steps` AggregateFunction(sum, UInt64),
    `jobs` AggregateFunction(sum, UInt64),
    `jobs_succeeded` AggregateFunction(sum, UInt64),
    `jobs_failed` AggregateFunction(sum, UInt64),
    `documents_out` AggregateFunction(sum, UInt64),
    `documents_indexed` AggregateFunction(sum, UInt64),
    `input_bytes` AggregateFunction(sum, UInt64),
    `duration_ms` AggregateFunction(sum, UInt64),
    `llm_input_tokens` AggregateFunction(sum, UInt64),
    `llm_output_tokens` AggregateFunction(sum, UInt64),
    `llm_requests` AggregateFunction(sum, UInt64),
    `audio_seconds` AggregateFunction(sum, Float64),
    `pages` AggregateFunction(sum, UInt64),
    `images` AggregateFunction(sum, UInt64),
    `external_requests` AggregateFunction(sum, UInt64)

ENGINE "AggregatingMergeTree"
ENGINE_SORTING_KEY "project_id, day, pipeline_uid, plugin"
ENGINE_PARTITION_KEY "toYYYYMM(day)"
ENGINE_TTL "day + INTERVAL 180 DAY"
